{
  "headline": "FDA's records trace our supply to a plant classified OAI 764 days before the posting",
  "headline_cites": ["D25"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA first posted the lidocaine hydrochloride shortage on 2012-02-22 and it remains Current as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["E81", "E71"]
    },
    {
      "text": "An FDA inspection of Hospira, Inc. (FEI 1021343) ended 2010-01-19 and was classified OAI with six observations on control procedures, in-process specifications, and dissemination of problem information.",
      "cites": ["E56"]
    },
    {
      "text": "That OAI inspection occurred 764 days before the shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["D25"]
    },
    {
      "text": "A Warning Letter was issued to Hospira, Inc. on 2010-04-12, 681 days before the posting.",
      "cites": ["D26", "E65"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Additional OAI inspections of Hospira, Inc. followed in 2011-06-17 (250 days before posting) and 2011-08-04 (202 days before posting).",
      "cites": ["D27", "D29", "E58", "E60"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Our Corvale East, Corvale General, and Corvale Lakeside sites all hold lidocaine hydrochloride 20 mg/mL 50 mL vials labeled by Hikma Pharmaceuticals USA Inc. (NDC 00143-9575-10).",
      "cites": ["E1", "E8", "E13"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rule-based best option is to transfer 40 vials of 20 mg/mL 50 mL from Corvale East (18.9 days on hand) to Corvale Lakeside (3.9 days on hand), which would give Lakeside 14 days of supply while East retains two weeks.",
      "cites": ["D1", "D3", "D39"]
    }
  ]
}
